// wdoc standard library — review comments.
//
// `@comment` records a review note in the source. It is written by
// `wcl wdoc serve --comment` (the dev server injects a JS client that lets
// you click a rendered block, or the page, and leave a note) and read back
// by `wcl wdoc comments` so an AI agent can act on the notes and then
// `wcl wdoc comments resolve <id>` to delete them.
//
// A comment attaches to a *real, editable* source block in one of three
// shapes (see `crates/wcl_wdoc/src/comments.rs`):
//
//   - on a hand-authored block directly      → `@comment(id=…, body=…)`
//   - on the enclosing `page`, for a block    → `@comment(id=…, body=…,
//     produced by a repeater/component           loc="0/2/1", target="…")`
//   - on the `page` as a whole (generic)      → `@comment(id=…, body=…)`  (no loc)
//
//   @comment(id="c12ab3", body="tighten this heading") heading "Install" { … }

namespace wdoc

@decorator("comment")
type Comment {
  id: utf8            // stable handle; survives edits so `resolve` can find it
  body: utf8          // the reviewer's note
  author: utf8?       // who left it
  status: symbol?     // :open (default) / :resolved
  loc: utf8?          // positional locator within the page (page-attached only)
  target: utf8?       // auto description of the referenced generated block
  quote: utf8?        // exact text the reviewer had highlighted when commenting
  page: utf8?         // resolved page name the comment was made on (scopes it to
                      // a single generated page whose source label can't resolve)
}
